# Managed by Ansible - do not edit manually
# Deny network egress (local IPC stays allowed) - /etc/apparmor.d/abstractions/local_mixin_network_deny
#
# Include in local-only viewers (image / video / PDF / score) that must have no
# network egress. Denies the egress families (inet / inet6) so connectivity stays
# blocked even if some abstraction pulls in a `network inet ...` allow later (e.g.
# abstractions/nameservice grants `network inet stream,`).
#
# NOT a bare `deny network,`: at abi/4.0+ AppArmor mediates AF_UNIX separately from the
# coarse `network` rule, and the apps that include this (Wayland / D-Bus / audio / journald
# clients) still need local IPC. local_mixin_network_local_ipc grants only AF_UNIX (no
# egress); the deny lines below block the actual network families. Obscure attack-surface
# families (rds / rxrpc / alg / ax25 / can ...) are not granted by anything these viewers
# include, so they stay default-denied without an explicit deny line here.
#
# Only effective when the including profile compiles at an abi that mediates network
# (abi/4.0+); managed profiles pin `abi <abi/5.0>` in their preamble for this.
#
# Plain `deny` (NOT `audit deny`): startup network probes (NSS, proxy autodetect) are
# routine noise, not a tripwire - silence them so the real `audit deny` tripwires stay
# visible. See "audit deny vs plain deny" in roles/apparmor/CLAUDE.md.
#include <abstractions/local_mixin_network_local_ipc>
deny network inet,
deny network inet6,
# Qt's bearer / network-status thread probes an AF_UNSPEC dgram socket every few
# seconds - already blocked; this silences the recurring create-denied spam.
deny network unspec,
